WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.900
Keep working when a provider runs out.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.871
This greet-app thread runs on Claude Code.

3
00:00:06.871 --> 00:00:11.220
It finished T-01 of the increment, and one task is left.

4
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.811
Ask for T-02, and Claude Code stops on its usage limit.

5
00:00:15.811 --> 00:00:19.782
Here the limit is simulated with SpecWithCode's test switch.

6
00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:24.710
The banner shows the reset time, and that the project rule continues with Codex.

7
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.244
Under the default rule, Switch automatically,

8
00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:31.559
SpecWithCode hands the stopped turn to Codex,

9
00:00:31.559 --> 00:00:34.143
with its context, in the same worktree.

10
00:00:34.143 --> 00:00:39.056
The row saying Usage limit resolved only means this chat continued.

11
00:00:39.056 --> 00:00:41.980
Claude Code stays limited until the reset.

12
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:45.659
Codex runs npm test and commits the change.

13
00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:49.105
Then, unasked, it runs specweave handoff.

14
00:00:49.105 --> 00:00:54.021
Its summary: T-02 is done on main, and all four tests pass.

15
00:00:54.021 --> 00:00:56.459
The plan shows both tasks done.

16
00:00:56.459 --> 00:01:00.580
One catch in this build: the picker then flips back to Claude Code,

17
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.740
so check it before your next message.

18
00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.585
In a terminal, specweave task list reads the ledger:

19
00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:08.630
Claude finished T-01,

20
00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.110
and Codex finished T-02,

21
00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.155
each with the test run that proved it.

22
00:01:13.155 --> 00:01:15.910
Both agents' commits are on the branch.

23
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.628
Set the rule per project, under Usage limits:

24
00:01:19.628 --> 00:01:24.089
switch automatically, offer the fallback, or wait for the reset.

25
00:01:24.089 --> 00:01:29.143
With Offer the fallback, nothing moves until you choose Continue with Codex.

26
00:01:29.143 --> 00:01:33.380
An idle thread can also move early, at 5% left.

27
00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.580
Next, sw-done verifies and closes the increment.
